# polls (rung 3) — A votes, B votes, A undoes, and B's vote survives.
#
# This is the rung's headline design record. examples/polls/README.md's
# "What to implement" step 5 records why UndoLastVoteChange is a *compensating
# action* rather than SessionLog::undoLast(): undoLast pops the newest entry
# regardless of who wrote it, so A's undo would have killed B's vote. The
# README names this exact interleaving as the test whose outcome is the
# design record.
#
# Here it is out of process, on two sockets, which is the shape a real pair of
# participants has and the shape the in-process interleaving test cannot take.
#
# The order is load-bearing: B's vote is the *newest* entry when A undoes. An
# undo that popped the newest entry would take B's, and the assertion that
# catches it is the one on B's count after the undo -- not the one on A's.
#
# Re-runnable: the poll is created here.

model PollModel

client alice

do CreatePoll title="Whose undo is it" options=[{"label":"Left"},{"label":"Right"}]
expect ok capture poll=$.pollId

do OpenPoll pollId=$poll
expect ok capture left=$.options[0].id
expect ok capture right=$.options[1].id

# ── A votes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
do SubmitVotes participantName=alice votes=[{"optionId":$left,"choice":"Yes"}]
expect ok

# ── B votes, and is now the newest entry in the log ────────────────────────
client bob

do OpenPoll pollId=$poll
expect ok

do SubmitVotes participantName=bob votes=[{"optionId":$right,"choice":"Yes"}]
expect ok

do GetPollState
expect ok field options[0].yesCount.num == 1
expect ok field options[1].yesCount.num == 1

# ── A undoes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
use alice

do UndoLastVoteChange participantName=alice
expect ok field restored == Yes

# A's vote is gone...
do GetPollState
expect ok field options[0].yesCount.num == 0
# ...and B's is untouched. This is the assertion the whole design decision is
# about: a principal-blind undo would have taken this one instead.
expect ok field options[1].yesCount.num == 1
expect ok field votes ~ "\"participantName\":\"bob\""
expect ok field votes !~ "\"participantName\":\"alice\""

# ── An undo with nothing of its own to undo is refused, not silently applied
# to someone else's change ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
do UndoLastVoteChange participantName=carol
expect err message == "nothing to undo for this participant"

# B's vote still stands after that refusal, too.
do GetPollState
expect ok field options[1].yesCount.num == 1
